#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049099 :topic/id #uuid "da82e0bb-7193-5348-9d38-5f5b8f5913d8" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152284 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151994 :question/id #uuid "4739ced1-bbcc-516b-971f-a580ec97961a" :question/math-academy-id "e-6861" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\ny'' + y' - 2y =0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny = Ae^{x} + Be^{- 2 x},\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\ny'' + y' - 2y =0,\n\\ \\ y(1) = e, \\ \\ y'(1) = e ^{-2}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(1)=e$ into our general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}e & =A{e}^{1}+B{e}^{-2(1)} \\\\ e & =Ae+B{e}^{-2} \\\\ A & =1-B{e}^{-3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition $y'(1) = e^{-2},$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\ny' = Ae^x - 2Be^{-2x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $y'(1)=e^{-2}$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-2} & =A{e}^{1}-2B{e}^{-2(1)} \\\\ {e}^{-2} & =Ae-2B{e}^{-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPutting the two equations from above together, we have the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}A &=1-B{e}^{-3} \\\\ {e}^{-2} &=Ae-2B{e}^{-2}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A = 1 - B e ^{-3}$ in the second equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-2} & =(1-B{e}^{-3})e-2B{e}^{-2} \\\\ 1 & ={e}^{3}-B-2B \\\\ B & =\\frac{{e}^{3}-1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, substituting $B= \\dfrac {e ^ 3 - 1} 3$ back into the equation $A = 1-Be^{-3}$ gives\n\n$$\nA = 1 -  \\dfrac {(e ^ 3 - 1) e ^ {-3}} 3 =   \\dfrac {2 +  e ^ {-3}} 3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution of the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny =  \\dfrac {  e ^ {-3} + 2} 3  e^{x} + \\dfrac {e ^ 3 - 1} 3 e^{-2x}.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b627c23d-f87b-5fd9-8e53-f2464eecff4d" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152401 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e031bec-4024-5bff-a0a7-6c68243bedda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431484} {:answer/id #uuid "a8b5524f-6144-5f88-9a69-8e05643972e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431493} {:answer/id #uuid "b8613441-e69b-5939-ae74-8cc30a7bd06d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4{e}^{-x}-3{e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431499} {:answer/id #uuid "ed6783de-fb3d-5d54-8286-c1aa1c50555e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{e}^{-x}-{e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431514} {:answer/id #uuid "f1cb52c6-ae5e-5d19-9335-21304dab5d85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-x}+2{e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431516}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed6783de-fb3d-5d54-8286-c1aa1c50555e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{e}^{-x}-{e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431514} :answer-field/id #uuid "3cd7eb07-6ad6-5159-a544-24234ed2ccad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148937}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "93cffb5e-8615-53c1-a574-533e068512ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-130343" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-{y}^{′}-2y=0,\\,y(0)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-4.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}-2{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -2) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -2 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -2)=0,\n$$\n\nand so $\\lambda =-1$ or $\\lambda =2.$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-x}+B{e}^{2x}.\n$$\n\nNow let us find constants $A$ and $B.$ \n\nSubstituting $y(0)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA+B=1.\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=-4.$ First, we differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}$:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-A{e}^{-x}+2B{e}^{2x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=-4$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n-A+2B=-4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following system of equations for $A$ and $B$:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}A+B &=1 \\\\ -A+2B &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=2,B=-1.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=2{e}^{-x}-{e}^{2x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152777 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1dabdd0c-2588-5f7d-8ccd-b68af2421ea7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=7{e}^{-3x}-10{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342485} {:answer/id #uuid "49169b95-990f-59eb-8bb6-9cf98419ab8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3{e}^{-3x}-6{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342839} {:answer/id #uuid "a4feee5b-c504-529a-b361-ad69aa51b813" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-12{e}^{-3x}+9{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343692} {:answer/id #uuid "c6148395-0be0-5c18-b79a-ca9ffdf1bf78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-10{e}^{-3x}+7{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343975} {:answer/id #uuid "eb97d4ca-37d6-530d-8bb6-f0f612d82f07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-9{e}^{-3x}+6{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344301}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6148395-0be0-5c18-b79a-ca9ffdf1bf78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-10{e}^{-3x}+7{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343975} :answer-field/id #uuid "18454ee3-e909-5372-948f-8f633a9d0c9f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344531}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "de2c9bcd-a587-5660-97a8-aa4955c427cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-7788" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+7{y}^{′}+12y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{-4x},\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+7{y}^{′}+12y=0,\\,y(0)=-3,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=2.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=-3$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA+B=-3.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=2,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-3A{e}^{-3x}-4B{e}^{-4x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(0)=2$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n-3A-4B=2.\n$$\n\nPutting the two equations from above together, we have the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}A+B &=-3 \\\\ -3A-4B &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=-10,B=7.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-10{e}^{-3x}+7{e}^{-4x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345349 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20709554-99f3-56be-8db0-e0eb104e22da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4{e}^{-3x}-2{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342505} {:answer/id #uuid "84bbff61-6dd6-5dae-8917-44ead432bf05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=5{e}^{-2x+2}-3{e}^{7x-7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343373} {:answer/id #uuid "974b02d5-ce48-565e-ac84-17370d67e1a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-2x+2}+{e}^{7x-7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343565} {:answer/id #uuid "a2f6aab0-8368-5237-9d3f-acd4dd4686c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4{e}^{-2x+2}-2{e}^{7x-7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343668} {:answer/id #uuid "d8253bb3-ebb4-55c1-b1e5-02305a7dfdb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{3x-3}+{e}^{4x-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344140}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "974b02d5-ce48-565e-ac84-17370d67e1a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-2x+2}+{e}^{7x-7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343565} :answer-field/id #uuid "be023620-9f23-57b8-b330-3195dfdaa3b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344827}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "fdf2426a-3d50-5569-9ef4-40597922e38a" :question/math-academy-id "q-7790" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-5{y}^{′}-14y=0,\\,y(1)=2,\\text{ }\\text{ }{y}^{′}(1)=5.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-5\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}-14{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda -14) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda -14 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -7)=0,\n$$\n\nand so $\\lambda =-2$ or $\\lambda =7.$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{7x}.\n$$\n\nNow let us find constants $A$ and $B.$ \n\nSubstituting $y(1)=2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA{e}^{-2}+B{e}^{7}=2.\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(1)=5.$ First, we differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}$:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-2A{e}^{-2x}+7B{e}^{7x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(1)=5$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n-2A{e}^{-2}+7B{e}^{7}=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following system of equations for $A$ and $B$:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}A{e}^{-2}+B{e}^{7} &=2 \\\\ -2A{e}^{-2}+7B{e}^{7} &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A={e}^{2},B={e}^{-7}.$\n\nNow we get the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={e}^{2}\\cdot {e}^{-2x}+{e}^{-7}\\cdot {e}^{7x} \\\\ y & ={e}^{-2x+2}+{e}^{7x-7}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357618 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e9e935d-a5d7-5060-9e81-1e294d0980f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2{e}^{3x}+4{e}^{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354802} {:answer/id #uuid "5022596d-970f-5ced-8b90-cbaea34880da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3{e}^{3x}-{e}^{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355379} {:answer/id #uuid "a73bc73f-cf6e-52ad-94d6-75b82cb2770c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-4{e}^{3x}+6{e}^{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356145} {:answer/id #uuid "e9a3407e-598c-5111-a3d5-936dd3cbe1ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{3x}+{e}^{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356707} {:answer/id #uuid "ecc8d744-46c1-577f-9579-6809c30034ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4{e}^{3x}-2{e}^{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356729}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ecc8d744-46c1-577f-9579-6809c30034ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4{e}^{3x}-2{e}^{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356729} :answer-field/id #uuid "81894cf1-2e76-58e4-9ee1-8ca4439b1de3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357147}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "54ccfb65-7e54-5949-bba7-09339d2681aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-94006" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-8{y}^{′}+15y=0,\\,y(0)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=2.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the roots of the characteristic polynomial:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-8\\lambda +15 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -5) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =3,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{3x}+B{e}^{5x}.\n$$\n\nNow we find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA+B=2.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=2,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=3A{e}^{3x}+5B{e}^{5x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(0)=2$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n3A+5B=2.\n$$\n\nPutting the two equations from above together, we have the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}A+B &=2 \\\\ 3A+5B &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=4,B=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =4{e}^{3x}-2{e}^{5x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357619 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19a1efcc-a84f-5cca-9296-2b025bda328f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=6{e}^{2x}+3{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354893} {:answer/id #uuid "82734f7f-fa07-5c61-ba7e-22e87bd268c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=5{e}^{2x}+4{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355810} {:answer/id #uuid "8c86721d-327c-5baf-aabe-7912a39c6df3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{e}^{2x}+7{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355905} {:answer/id #uuid "9885b9f4-86ac-562b-854d-b75ade26747c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=8{e}^{2x}+{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356014} {:answer/id #uuid "e5e25ae2-343f-5e58-90b5-7d716302e8ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{2x}+8{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356672}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19a1efcc-a84f-5cca-9296-2b025bda328f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=6{e}^{2x}+3{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354893} :answer-field/id #uuid "64d9a0b2-d2bc-591c-a9ff-76719c9b090c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357091}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a1ea3f1a-b518-5ab9-b9f1-47877b73191f" :question/math-academy-id "q-94007" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-6{y}^{′}+8y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{2x}+B{e}^{4x},\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-6{y}^{′}+8y=0,\\,y(0)=9,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=24.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=9$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA+B=9.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=24,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2A{e}^{2x}+4B{e}^{4x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(0)=24$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2A+4B & =24 \\\\ A+2B & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPutting the two equations from above together, we have the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}A+B &=9 \\\\ A+2B &=12\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=6,B=3.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=6{e}^{2x}+3{e}^{4x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357622 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0545280c-b50e-55cd-8cb1-5a42f78528e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{e}^{-5x}-5{e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354698} {:answer/id #uuid "3975197f-9978-546b-9c3f-ef37ec77e943" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3{e}^{-5x}-6{e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355182} {:answer/id #uuid "97040bc1-30c6-53ac-85f7-eca6a0c462db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-5x}-2{e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355989} {:answer/id #uuid "b7d335b3-afcf-545b-b4b7-ca2138e97c3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-5x}-4{e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356275} {:answer/id #uuid "cdbefa9e-ecaa-5525-9176-66433d843d61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-5{e}^{-5x}+2{e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3975197f-9978-546b-9c3f-ef37ec77e943" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3{e}^{-5x}-6{e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355182} :answer-field/id #uuid "cdf5ed7f-cd47-5b1b-a5a6-654871efb947" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357292}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "16b6daa1-1a79-55ed-98ca-cc102191facb" :question/math-academy-id "q-94011" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+7{y}^{′}+10y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-5x}+B{e}^{-2x},\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+7{y}^{′}+10y=0,\\,y(0)=-3,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-3.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=-3$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA+B=-3.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=-3,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-5A{e}^{-5x}-2B{e}^{-2x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(0)=-3$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n-5A-2B=-3.\n$$\n\nPutting the two equations from above together, we have the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}A+B &=-3 \\\\ -5A-2B &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=3,B=-6.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=3{e}^{-5x}-6{e}^{-2x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431538 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "419e161a-490d-5c6f-a7e4-eaa1b01c0887" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431471} {:answer/id #uuid "596a6ddd-3d0f-5678-9be7-860b0f40740a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-3x}+3{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431478} {:answer/id #uuid "9d1aafac-6504-5529-8eb6-e512b18e650b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=5{e}^{-3x}-3{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431491} {:answer/id #uuid "ebfe6c00-24b3-5751-94bf-30b104f0e51e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431512} {:answer/id #uuid "ef9a2e7c-4ae2-58e1-bf2d-a13b03f1e88d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-3x}+{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431515}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef9a2e7c-4ae2-58e1-bf2d-a13b03f1e88d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-3x}+{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431515} :answer-field/id #uuid "65f2e16b-2b82-5cc9-a8ad-cf8d984e234d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431524}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "cbabadfa-0d4d-5a45-80b7-bf364847e945" :question/math-academy-id "q-130339" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-9y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{3x},\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-9y=0,\\,y(0)=2,\\text{ }\\text{ }{y}^{′}(0)=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA+B=2.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=0,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-3A{e}^{-3x}+3B{e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(0)=0$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n-3A+3B=0.\n$$\n\nPutting the two equations from above together, we have the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}A+B &=2 \\\\ -3A+3B &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=1,B=1.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-3x}+{e}^{3x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431539 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d40d78b-f10f-551a-bf45-f2b3a9619d8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-x}-{e}^{8x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431460} {:answer/id #uuid "1029e982-1cb8-59a1-800a-6eddc8bb0c8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{e}^{-x}-2{e}^{8x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431462} {:answer/id #uuid "204931ce-cb59-5974-b135-26060d7cd2da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3{e}^{-x}-3{e}^{8x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431466} {:answer/id #uuid "4e18fb50-aa99-53db-bb7e-d22c8a9849c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2{e}^{-x}+2{e}^{8x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431475} {:answer/id #uuid "8d32c42c-4dc2-5fb7-b932-58cc4bb05b0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{8x}-{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431487}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1029e982-1cb8-59a1-800a-6eddc8bb0c8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{e}^{-x}-2{e}^{8x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431462} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b57be19-b31a-5529-8b7d-a45f836917f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431525}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d99b4ca2-1051-5b19-b0ca-e022766a3c13" :question/math-academy-id "q-130340" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-7{y}^{′}-8y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-x}+B{e}^{8x},\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-7{y}^{′}-8y=0,\\,y(0)=0,\\text{ }\\text{ }{y}^{′}(0)=-18.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA+B=0.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=-18,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-A{e}^{-x}+8B{e}^{8x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(0)=-18$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n-A+8B=-18.\n$$\n\nPutting the two equations from above together, we have the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}A+B &=0 \\\\ 8B-A &=-18\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=2,B=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=2{e}^{-x}-2{e}^{8x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431541 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26037b2c-fdab-548c-ba39-81bdf3515e82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-3x}+2{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431467} {:answer/id #uuid "7569b8e5-0cd2-5f8b-acf3-e84018c38232" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-5x+5}+2{e}^{x-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431486} {:answer/id #uuid "bc750cc4-f587-579a-b2ff-04773b6d8134" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2{e}^{-5x+5}+3{e}^{x-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431501} {:answer/id #uuid "d405ca87-259a-5550-ad19-3cb0d9609b6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3{e}^{4x-4}-2{e}^{x-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431508} {:answer/id #uuid "ec87e771-a6a7-53b3-8bba-b2c753c87011" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-7{e}^{-5x+5}+8{e}^{x-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431513}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7569b8e5-0cd2-5f8b-acf3-e84018c38232" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-5x+5}+2{e}^{x-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431486} :answer-field/id #uuid "028dd5c8-1b67-5564-af86-02df34d419e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431520}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "fe7e11df-3bda-53fa-998a-37d8783a4f32" :question/math-academy-id "q-7789" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}-5y=0,\\,y(1)=1,\\text{ }\\text{ }{y}^{′}(1)=7.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the roots of the characteristic polynomial:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda -5 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +5)(\\lambda -1) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =-5,1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-5x}+B{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nNow we find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(1)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA{e}^{-5}+Be=1.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(1)=7,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-5A{e}^{-5x}+B{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(1)=7$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n-5A{e}^{-5}+Be=7.\n$$\n\nPutting the two equations from above together, we have the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}A{e}^{-5}+Be &=1 \\\\ -5A{e}^{-5}+Be &=7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=-{e}^{5},B=2{e}^{-1}.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-{e}^{5}\\cdot {e}^{-5x}+2{e}^{-1}\\cdot {e}^{x} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-5x+5}+2{e}^{x-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving Second-Order IVPs When the Characteristic Equation Has Distinct Real Roots"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152285 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151995 :question/id #uuid "95cdd4cc-df70-5dac-8bd3-66edb012cdcb" :question/math-academy-id "e-6862" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\ny'' - 4 y' + 4y =0,\n\\qquad y(0) =  3, \\qquad y'(0) = 2.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the roots of the characteristic polynomial:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +4 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -2)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have a repeated root $\\lambda = 2,$ so we have the following general solution:\n\n$$\ny = A e ^ { 2 x} + B x e ^ {2 x}\n$$\n\nWe find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=3$ into our general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 & =A{e}^{2(0)}+B(0){e}^{2(0)} \\\\ 3 & =A{e}^{0}+0 \\\\ 3 & =A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition $y' (0) = 2,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\ny'  = 2 A e ^ {2 x} +  B e ^ { 2 x} + 2 B x e ^{ 2 x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $y'(0)=2$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =2A{e}^{2(0)}+B{e}^{2(0)}+2B(0){e}^{2(0)} \\\\ 2 & =2A{e}^{0}+B{e}^{0}+0 \\\\ 2 & =2A+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPutting the two equations from above together, we have the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3 &=A \\\\ 2 &=2A+B\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=3$ into the second equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =6+B \\\\ B & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $A=3$ and $B=-4,$ and therefore the solution is \n\n$$\ny = 3 e ^ { 2 x } - 4 x e ^ { 2 x}.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84e87d0d-806d-5587-849e-17d6999dbbd1" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152402 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0843ecfa-4e3a-592f-95c8-ebdbd00c572f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2{e}^{-3x}-x{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431457} {:answer/id #uuid "0922b0c1-b8d5-5acc-824f-3d66df13cd2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2{e}^{-3x}-4x{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431459} {:answer/id #uuid "3dbb7a89-524b-5fb7-8987-365ee58f1aac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2{e}^{3x}+2x{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431469} {:answer/id #uuid "af81ca3e-eea1-5fa8-b729-88ef645ad2ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2{e}^{3x}-x{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431498} {:answer/id #uuid "f7aec91b-5023-511f-94e5-52c5a358d29c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2{e}^{-3x}+8x{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431517}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0922b0c1-b8d5-5acc-824f-3d66df13cd2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2{e}^{-3x}-4x{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431459} :answer-field/id #uuid "e82527bc-a697-52b6-866e-a3ae6fadb46e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148943}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "da0e1bd5-5ab3-52c5-b411-da88433bbf6c" :question/math-academy-id "q-130346" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+6{y}^{′}+9y=0,\\,y(0)=-2,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=2.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the roots of the characteristic polynomial:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +9 & =0 \\\\ {(\\lambda +3)}^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have a repeated root $\\lambda =-3,$ so we have the following general solution:\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-3x}+Bx{e}^{-3x}\n$$\n\nWe find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=-2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA=-2.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=2,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-3A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{-3x}-3Bx{e}^{-3x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(0)=2$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n-3A+B=2.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $A=-2$ gives $B=-4.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-2{e}^{-3x}-4x{e}^{-3x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152779 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b84d0516-abe6-519f-8b0b-3cfa502bafc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 5e^{-5x} + 28xe^{-5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151182} {:answer/id #uuid "fecd06bf-6d1f-5b42-93af-6e13a6dc6a3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 5e^{-5x} + 20xe^{-5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151183} {:answer/id #uuid "307a4c35-5bf4-51b8-9ebb-a265cf6efbc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 5e^{-5x} + 12xe^{-5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151184} {:answer/id #uuid "498ea3a8-9728-5385-968d-996768552371" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 5e^{-5x} + 42xe^{-5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151185} {:answer/id #uuid "74d94883-b4ae-54ac-9c75-c13e01009e0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 5e^{-5x} + 22xe^{-5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151186}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "498ea3a8-9728-5385-968d-996768552371" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 5e^{-5x} + 42xe^{-5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151185} :answer-field/id #uuid "649939b1-717e-5219-8a42-3f52dce1bd13" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151181}] :question/id #uuid "93338c02-7761-5a7e-bb19-c834b8f78250" :question/math-academy-id "q-7814" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n$y^{″} + 10y^{′} + 25y = 0$\n\nhas the general solution\n$y = Ae^{-5x} + Bxe^{-5x}$,\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n$$\n\\displaystyle y^{″} + 10y^{′} + 25y = 0, y(0) = 5, y^{′}(0) = 17.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The characteristic equation is\n$$\n\\lambda^2+10\\lambda+25=(\\lambda+5)^2=0.\n$$\nThe repeated root $-5$ gives $y=Ae^{-5x}+Bxe^{-5x}.$ From $y(0)=5,$ we obtain $A=5.$ Differentiating gives\n$$\ny'=-5Ae^{-5x}+Be^{-5x}-5Bxe^{-5x}.\n$$\nUsing $y'(0)=17$ yields $-5A+B=17,$ so $B=42.$ Therefore,\n$$\ny=5e^{-5x}+42xe^{-5x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265888 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3036bc4c-9a29-58e4-9e4f-63ea2676c1e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=5{e}^{10x}+2{e}^{-10x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263408} {:answer/id #uuid "55af75d9-3215-505e-a2e4-e26268f9030c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-5{e}^{10x}+x{e}^{10x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263736} {:answer/id #uuid "d919ddf6-f89c-58df-a15e-862e986084bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=5{e}^{-10x}+27x{e}^{-10x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264893} {:answer/id #uuid "ee688c23-1e67-57ab-a381-db1024fe901c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=5{e}^{-10x}+45x{e}^{-10x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265085} {:answer/id #uuid "fc4f0037-a17d-55e5-848d-2223ac9f5d18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=5{e}^{-10x}+x{e}^{-10x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265215}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee688c23-1e67-57ab-a381-db1024fe901c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=5{e}^{-10x}+45x{e}^{-10x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265085} :answer-field/id #uuid "5902029f-b097-505e-a6b6-62abfadc46aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265400}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9e9e8cdd-f777-54e6-9fd2-e5cfbbe99eb7" :question/math-academy-id "q-130345" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+20{y}^{′}+100y=0,\\,y(0)=5,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-5.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the roots of the characteristic polynomial:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+20\\lambda +100 & =0 \\\\ {(\\lambda +10)}^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have a repeated root $\\lambda =-10,$ so we have the following general solution:\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-10x}+Bx{e}^{-10x}\n$$\n\nWe find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=5$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA=5.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=-5,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-10A{e}^{-10x}+B{e}^{-10x}-10Bx{e}^{-10x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(0)=-5$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n-10A+B=-5.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $A=5$ gives $B=45.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=5{e}^{-10x}+45x{e}^{-10x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265889 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36c5b469-6463-52a3-9811-47c75a31bfcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-4x}-3x{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263485} {:answer/id #uuid "60243a49-cda4-50c0-b8ca-f4c51611f0c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-4x}-x{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263831} {:answer/id #uuid "63d7d82b-1867-5e2b-946e-a2fe092e42b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-4x}-2x{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263863} {:answer/id #uuid "70efef71-e27a-55bf-87a3-0c9313933ac0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-4x}+2x{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263977} {:answer/id #uuid "ab769ccf-0d36-5207-ae5a-dd9a01627f58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-4x}+x{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264474}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70efef71-e27a-55bf-87a3-0c9313933ac0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-4x}+2x{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263977} :answer-field/id #uuid "f859fd31-fcdc-565a-badb-2939009738ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265688}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4fdb5918-7d82-5692-8ab6-ddec209bc201" :question/math-academy-id "q-130348" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+8{y}^{′}+16y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-4x}+Bx{e}^{-4x},\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+8{y}^{′}+16y=0,\\,y(0)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-2.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA=1.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=-2,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-4A{e}^{-4x}+B{e}^{-4x}-4Bx{e}^{-4x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=-2$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n-4A+B=-2.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $A=1$ gives $B=2.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-4x}+2x{e}^{-4x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335796 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2409f788-25c2-5cf1-92db-fc815b9311d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{4x}+2x{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333323} {:answer/id #uuid "2a7bacfe-fc07-50ef-9d2a-228b7bf2edb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{4x}-5x{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333391} {:answer/id #uuid "d454f930-45db-5273-b06f-29cefe1fcc9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{4x}-x{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334850} {:answer/id #uuid "dcf0c645-0f9d-5637-a9fd-b6f8ddaf88b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{4x}-6x{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334920} {:answer/id #uuid "e037d7ea-fe0e-5526-a8aa-616389bb432a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{4x}+4x{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334938}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a7bacfe-fc07-50ef-9d2a-228b7bf2edb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{4x}-5x{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333391} :answer-field/id #uuid "861329c9-3fed-5eb9-b7f7-7c50805ac43d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335494}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7f8e3298-7918-50f3-9ceb-e26ca6656ff1" :question/math-academy-id "q-65116" :question/problem "Given that the functions  ${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{4x}$ and ${y}_{2}(x)=x{e}^{4x}$ are solutions to the equation ${y}^{″}-8{y}^{′}+16y=0,$ solve the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-8{y}^{′}+16y=0,\\,y(0)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-1.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "According to the superposition principle, any linear combination of the functions  ${y}_{1}(x)$  and ${y}_{2}(x)$  must be a solution to the original differential equation.\n\nHence, the general solution is: \n\n$$\ny={c}_{1}{e}^{4x}+{c}_{2}x{e}^{4x}\n$$\n\nNow, we find constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ \n\nSubstituting $y(0)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=1.\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=-1.$ First, we differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=(4{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}){e}^{4x}+4{c}_{2}x{e}^{4x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${c}_{1}=1$ and ${y}^{′}(0)=-1$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1=4(1)+{c}_{2}\\,⟹\\,{c}_{2}=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{4x}-5x{e}^{4x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348067 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29e8157a-552f-5c3e-9922-5f98c42236bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2{e}^{x/2-1}+3x{e}^{x/2-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345723} {:answer/id #uuid "2aa6a344-1c11-5d1d-91e2-7b17d052e60c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=x{e}^{-3x/2+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345730} {:answer/id #uuid "3fb0744b-1328-5467-aff8-5eda9102546f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-3x/2+1}+2x{e}^{-3x/2+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345893} {:answer/id #uuid "5e98c6cd-0b58-542c-859e-0b8cec34dba1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{e}^{x/2-1}+2x{e}^{x/2-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346167} {:answer/id #uuid "8abde012-2b17-5b1a-afc7-33d35b8535b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3{e}^{-3x/2+1}-2x{e}^{-3x/2+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346552}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3fb0744b-1328-5467-aff8-5eda9102546f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-3x/2+1}+2x{e}^{-3x/2+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345893} :answer-field/id #uuid "db589b01-39df-5ab0-9143-384f9d7d07fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347992}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ece2165a-867c-5bfa-9095-1c580456d3cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-7815" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}+\\frac{9y}{4}=0,\\,y(1)={e}^{-1/2},\\text{ }\\text{ }{y}^{′}(1)=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-1/2}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+3\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+\\frac{9}{4}{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}\\left({\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda +\\frac{9}{4}\\right) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda +\\frac{9}{4} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left(\\lambda +\\frac{3}{2}\\right)\\left(\\lambda +\\frac{3}{2}\\right) & =0 \\\\ {\\left(\\lambda +\\frac{3}{2}\\right)}^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\lambda =-\\frac{3}{2}$ is a repeated root.\n\nSo the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-3x/2}+Bx{e}^{-3x/2}.\n$$\n\nLet us find constants $A$ and $B.$ \nSubstituting $y(1)={e}^{-1/2}$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{e}^{-3/2}+B{e}^{-3/2} & ={e}^{-1/2} \\\\ A+B & =e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(1)=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-1/2}.$ First, we differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}$:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-\\frac{3}{2}A{e}^{-3/2x}+B{e}^{-3/2x}-\\frac{3}{2}Bx{e}^{-3/2x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(1)=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-1/2}$ into the above gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2}A{e}^{-3/2}-\\frac{1}{2}B{e}^{-3/2} & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-1/2} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2}A-\\frac{1}{2}B & =\\frac{1}{2}e \\\\ -3A-B & =e\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following system of equations for $A$ and $B$:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}A+B &=e \\\\ -3A-B &=e\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=-e,B=2e.$\n\nNow we get the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-e\\cdot {e}^{-3x/2}+2e\\cdot x{e}^{-3x/2} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-3x/2+1}+2x{e}^{-3x/2+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357623 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22261154-e164-5f93-bca3-5795854513c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=8{e}^{-x}+4x{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354954} {:answer/id #uuid "798e95c5-d3f7-5738-8022-1f7507d566d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=8{e}^{-x}+8x{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355728} {:answer/id #uuid "7b2e9e24-1bdd-50eb-ad43-718710dfe81d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=8{e}^{-x}-8x{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355747} {:answer/id #uuid "832d8ead-8512-59b2-9e07-0bfd149d1118" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=8{e}^{-x}+6x{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355820} {:answer/id #uuid "cd829b4a-bab0-515b-9fd3-c59c2052469b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=8{e}^{-x}-4x{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356463}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "798e95c5-d3f7-5738-8022-1f7507d566d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=8{e}^{-x}+8x{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355728} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7f4ba42-f5f4-5ab8-9251-8cd947b91ff0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357328}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "996ecbd7-d457-5eef-ace4-2ef3cc5c9746" :question/math-academy-id "q-94017" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-x}+Bx{e}^{-x},\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+y=0,\\,y(0)=8,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=8$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA=8.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=0,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-A{e}^{-x}+B{e}^{-x}-Bx{e}^{-x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=0$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n-A+B=0.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $A=8$ gives $B=8.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=8{e}^{-x}+8x{e}^{-x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393765 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eeaa8919-6cd1-523d-89da-7ef2030fd077" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=11{e}^{4x-4}-9x{e}^{4x-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393767} {:answer/id #uuid "31ad293a-a2de-5b04-a010-75b1e574916b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-7{e}^{4x-4}+9x{e}^{4x-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393768} {:answer/id #uuid "0a7466a7-5e6b-57ce-b40f-1d86f392fa6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=5{e}^{4x-4}-3x{e}^{4x-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393769} {:answer/id #uuid "2731b0a9-3ca5-56a5-b3d2-8efcf3d3f0af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=8{e}^{2x-2}-6x{e}^{2x-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393770} {:answer/id #uuid "738f5cba-3a2c-5ec8-92f7-05586e62d819" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3{e}^{2x-2}-x{e}^{2x-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393771}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eeaa8919-6cd1-523d-89da-7ef2030fd077" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=11{e}^{4x-4}-9x{e}^{4x-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393767} :answer-field/id #uuid "656ffe0f-9fb3-55a1-98b5-b13db8a4f14b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393766}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e0ccd8f3-5c55-5b1e-8569-1f7045c0f609" :question/math-academy-id "q-7798" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-8{y}^{′}+16y=0,\\,y(1)=2,\\text{ }\\text{ }{y}^{′}(1)=-1.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-8\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+16{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-8\\lambda +16) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-8\\lambda +16 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -4) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -4)^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\lambda =4$ is a repeated root.\n\nSo the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{4x}+Bx{e}^{4x}.\n$$\n\nLet us find constants $A$ and $B.$ \n\nSubstituting $y(1)=2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA{e}^{4}+B{e}^{4}=2.\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(1)=-1.$ First, we differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}$:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=4A{e}^{4x}+B{e}^{4x}+4Bx{e}^{4x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(1)=-1$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n4A{e}^{4}+5B{e}^{4}=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following system of equations for $A$ and $B$:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}A{e}^{4}+B{e}^{4} &=2 \\\\ 4A{e}^{4}+5B{e}^{4} &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=11{e}^{-4},B=-9{e}^{-4}.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =11{e}^{-4}\\cdot {e}^{4x}-9{e}^{-4}\\cdot x{e}^{4x} \\\\  & =11{e}^{4x-4}-9x{e}^{4x-4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431533 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0137ee6e-c523-5606-ab61-bd96f6cd46e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-2x}+2x{e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431455} {:answer/id #uuid "1f869bf6-107f-5db7-b5a5-33d521155f66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-2x}+5x{e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431464} {:answer/id #uuid "42d8c8b0-9be5-591b-b0ec-8b768f062a61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{2x}+x{e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431472} {:answer/id #uuid "462f6db9-3bd4-53ff-a35f-8656edd69646" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-2x}+x{e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431474} {:answer/id #uuid "6bd8cda8-05fa-59b2-9091-e867beec2408" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{2x}-5x{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431483}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f869bf6-107f-5db7-b5a5-33d521155f66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-2x}+5x{e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431464} :answer-field/id #uuid "c771707c-db14-54e5-9719-2f5b8eb0740c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431530}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "385b9591-ad6c-5296-82bc-53313648dde5" :question/math-academy-id "q-7797" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}+4y=0,\\,y(0)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=3.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+4\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+4{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +4) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +4 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda +2) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +2)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\lambda =-2$ is a repeated root.\n\nSo the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-2x}+Bx{e}^{-2x}.\n$$\n\nNow let's find the constants $A$ and $B.$ \n\nSubstituting $y(0)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA=1.\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=3.$ First, we differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}$:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-2A{e}^{-2x}+-2Bx{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{-2x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=3$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n-2A+B=3.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $A=1$ gives $B=5.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-2x}+5x{e}^{-2x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431534 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "090f99d5-9625-5409-8bfa-8e2c4cd59aac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-7x}+8x{e}^{-7x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431458} {:answer/id #uuid "203c8f4e-c8c1-5cb3-9c03-69fcae139338" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-7x}-2x{e}^{-7x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431465} {:answer/id #uuid "419328d7-32fd-5588-ac38-f02df1730edf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-7x}-x{e}^{-7x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431470} {:answer/id #uuid "da315c42-36d1-50ab-b060-34532474faac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-7x}-7x{e}^{-7x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431511} {:answer/id #uuid "f7f42718-e600-5ca9-99e4-263408373f71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-7x}+x{e}^{-7x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431518}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7f42718-e600-5ca9-99e4-263408373f71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-7x}+x{e}^{-7x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431518} :answer-field/id #uuid "b628b5a8-23fe-5a39-8e61-e3f1bcd259c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431528}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4a808d33-3853-58bc-a004-7d852404000e" :question/math-academy-id "q-130347" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+14{y}^{′}+49y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-7x}+Bx{e}^{-7x},\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+14{y}^{′}+49y=0,\\,y(0)=-1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=8.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=-1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA=-1.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=8,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-7A{e}^{-7x}+B{e}^{-7x}-7Bx{e}^{-7x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=8$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n-7A+B=8.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $A=-1$ gives $B=1.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-{e}^{-7x}+x{e}^{-7x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476916 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "501007c1-1237-54a3-8146-49746a54174b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4{e}^{x}-4x{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476368} {:answer/id #uuid "6133a790-bf37-5624-a5e5-d93d8aac76a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4{e}^{x}+x{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476424} {:answer/id #uuid "90703a07-a49f-5b3e-9f80-5fb5897a85ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4{e}^{x}+2x{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476512} {:answer/id #uuid "e78a3592-edab-5dca-829b-212313e22fe6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4{e}^{x}+4x{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476720} {:answer/id #uuid "f6418223-cfc1-5b18-8627-68adb9ed9afd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4{e}^{x}+8x{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476746}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e78a3592-edab-5dca-829b-212313e22fe6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4{e}^{x}+4x{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476720} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca796d4b-8681-5245-bc1d-c35792d5e364" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476844}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7e57d61a-2fa5-55d2-aed6-295e67c97f51" :question/math-academy-id "q-130350" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}+y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{x}+Bx{e}^{x},\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}+y=0,\\,y(0)=4,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=8.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=4$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA=4.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=8,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=A{e}^{x}+B{e}^{x}+Bx{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=8$ into the above gives\n\n$$\nA+B=8.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $A=4$ gives $B=4.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=4{e}^{x}+4x{e}^{x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532656 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20d48bb0-1579-5910-bda9-3488cfc27188" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{e}^{5x}-9x{e}^{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531999} {:answer/id #uuid "364be568-53f5-599a-b8c5-5d41c25c736d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{e}^{5x}+6x{e}^{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532042} {:answer/id #uuid "644ffb41-3a13-5e6e-829b-683cb23cf0e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{e}^{5x}+x{e}^{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532155} {:answer/id #uuid "747e9c3b-3d01-5594-9408-b23ec8e2b378" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{e}^{5x}+3x{e}^{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532197} {:answer/id #uuid "f20309b5-4187-58b6-b1e7-3989a23ea58e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{e}^{5x}+4x{e}^{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532457}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "364be568-53f5-599a-b8c5-5d41c25c736d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{e}^{5x}+6x{e}^{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532042} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f3de0d8-361d-5e2c-a8ff-302d31ec457a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532530}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "534aed09-ef02-5ca1-a426-154a43b90b94" :question/math-academy-id "q-94015" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-10{y}^{′}+25y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{5x}+Bx{e}^{5x},\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-10{y}^{′}+25y=0,\\,y(0)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=16.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA=2.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=16,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=5A{e}^{5x}+B{e}^{5x}+5Bx{e}^{5x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=16$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n5A+B=16.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $A=2$ gives $B=6.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=2{e}^{5x}+6x{e}^{5x}.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving Second-Order IVPs When the Characteristic Equation Has Repeated Roots"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152286 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151983 :question/id #uuid "88fe37cf-5df2-5988-90b8-082f7aaca609" :question/math-academy-id "e-6791" :question/problem "Solve the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\ny'' + y = 0, \\quad y(\\pi) = 2, \\quad y'(\\pi) = -1\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the roots of the characteristic polynomial:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+1 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-1 \\\\ \\lambda  & =\\pm \\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following general solution:\n\n$$\ny = A \\cos x + B \\sin x\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find constants $A$ and $B.$ To do this, we apply the initial conditions $y(\\pi)=2,$ $y'(\\pi)=-1.$\n\n- Substituting $y(\\pi) = 2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(\\pi ) & =2 \\\\ A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi +B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi  & =2 \\\\ -A & =2 \\\\ A & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Computing $y'(x),$ we get\n\n$$\ny' =  - A \\sin{x} + B\\cos{x},\n$$\n\nand substituting $y'(\\pi)=-1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(\\pi ) & =-1 \\\\ -A\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi +B\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi  & =-1 \\\\ -B & =-1 \\\\ B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny = -2\\cos{x} + \\sin{x}.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8ebb2332-3e40-5627-bc43-258ca4a80424" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152403 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8bfc2fdb-4a42-5994-9537-e2225f8eb1f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 7\\cos (\\sqrt{11}x) - \\sqrt{11}\\sin (\\sqrt{11}x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148950} {:answer/id #uuid "e229a207-4ef2-5d22-867b-ccab34a24868" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 7\\cos (\\sqrt{11}x) - 4\\sin (\\sqrt{11}x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148951} {:answer/id #uuid "e946e55a-f081-5877-8dd6-33a721fca4e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 7\\cos (\\sqrt{11}x) + 2\\sin (\\sqrt{11}x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148952} {:answer/id #uuid "011457b9-c1fa-5467-be44-8de0b082eb4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 7\\cos (\\sqrt{11}x) - \\sin (\\sqrt{11}x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148953} {:answer/id #uuid "2c46909d-4cc1-5ebf-853b-6b12ed2aabb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 7\\cos (\\sqrt{11}x) - \\frac{4\\sqrt{11}}{11}\\sin (\\sqrt{11}x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148954}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e229a207-4ef2-5d22-867b-ccab34a24868" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 7\\cos (\\sqrt{11}x) - 4\\sin (\\sqrt{11}x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148951} :answer-field/id #uuid "c923a4d5-1e96-5cfb-9e2d-1463a34bb868" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148949}] :question/id #uuid "31316f4c-9980-5deb-aa03-fe5173062056" :question/math-academy-id "q-130365" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n$$\n\\displaystyle y^{″} + 11y = 0, y(0) = 7, y^{′}(0) =-4\\sqrt{11}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The characteristic roots are $\\lambda=\\pm\\sqrt{11}\\mathrm{i},$ giving\n$$\ny=P\\cos(\\sqrt{11}x)+Q\\sin(\\sqrt{11}x).\n$$\nThe first condition gives $P=7.$ Differentiating,\n$$\ny'=-\\sqrt{11}P\\sin(\\sqrt{11}x)+\\sqrt{11}Q\\cos(\\sqrt{11}x).\n$$\nThus $y'(0)=-4\\sqrt{11}$ gives $\\sqrt{11}Q=-4\\sqrt{11},$ so $Q=-4.$ Therefore,\n$$\ny=7\\cos(\\sqrt{11}x)-4\\sin(\\sqrt{11}x).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152639 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16afed35-5463-5e89-b46a-71267d7d4dfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333191} {:answer/id #uuid "c0d2b579-81ed-55f0-86c7-1541a3ed079c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334660} {:answer/id #uuid "f16df0e0-2094-5727-8779-eedca1e17dee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335105} {:answer/id #uuid "fc2ea755-747f-5b1b-81ec-4430d746d47b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335202} {:answer/id #uuid "fc44ffb2-d97c-5268-8493-a8451eaabd4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335206}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f16df0e0-2094-5727-8779-eedca1e17dee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335105} :answer-field/id #uuid "87dc976c-f470-53a5-ae6e-a363a677d1ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335500}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0006dc55-4e80-5e2f-bc47-1762d506390e" :question/math-academy-id "q-65117" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+16y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=A\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+B\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x,\n$$\n\nsolve the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+16y=0,\\,y(0)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-4.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=-4,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=4A\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x-4B\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=-4$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4=4A\\,⟹\\,A=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265890 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ca279fa-4ea3-5c16-9dc0-8620719f230e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡9x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263541} {:answer/id #uuid "6a505a18-e024-50e0-b80a-858fbcaa6bd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡9x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡9x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263914} {:answer/id #uuid "8cce89f9-bee9-5289-81c4-db3fae1227af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=9\\operatorname{sin}⁡9x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡9x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264205} {:answer/id #uuid "90b3b547-0fc6-5a96-a8f6-c08b53b59da0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡9x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡9x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264243} {:answer/id #uuid "d6ea9603-cfe9-587a-b7b0-4ca946cacc16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡9x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡9x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264870}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a505a18-e024-50e0-b80a-858fbcaa6bd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡9x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡9x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263914} :answer-field/id #uuid "17f89692-acb9-5d62-ad5f-fa9a68677812" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265283}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e3f2de60-d0ab-571c-bda3-5e60802fef2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-130353" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+81y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=A\\operatorname{sin}⁡9x+B\\operatorname{cos}⁡9x,\n$$\n\nsolve the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+81y=0,\\,y(0)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-9.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=-9,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=9A\\operatorname{cos}⁡9x-9B\\operatorname{sin}⁡9x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=-9$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9=9A\\,⟹\\,A=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡9x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡9x.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265891 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "265e1782-c5d3-5404-b0dc-1f238985c850" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡10x+10\\operatorname{sin}⁡10x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263332} {:answer/id #uuid "644cfb92-fba8-575e-a2e7-4eb31272b73b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡10x+10\\operatorname{sin}⁡10x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263868} {:answer/id #uuid "70fc997a-7346-5d08-8a26-7f2724e5123e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡10x+10\\operatorname{sin}⁡10x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263978} {:answer/id #uuid "84635d9e-764f-5b0d-bf9d-aa618bf4fd5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=10\\operatorname{cos}⁡10x+10\\operatorname{sin}⁡10x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264136} {:answer/id #uuid "d944bcf9-af4c-51bc-930a-1ea0792d0eb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=10\\operatorname{sin}⁡10x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264894}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "644cfb92-fba8-575e-a2e7-4eb31272b73b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡10x+10\\operatorname{sin}⁡10x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263868} :answer-field/id #uuid "17b36db8-e718-535a-864a-71cd83e3ed6d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265282}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "92c6e1b0-3483-5e66-a7f6-e095cce0e115" :question/math-academy-id "q-130355" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+100y=0,\\,y\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=10,\\,{y}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=50.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the roots of the characteristic polynomial:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+100 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-100 \\\\ \\lambda  & =\\pm 10\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =P\\operatorname{cos}⁡10x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡10x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe find the constants $P$ and $Q$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=10$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=50,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-10P\\operatorname{sin}⁡10x+10Q\\operatorname{cos}⁡10x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=50$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-10P=50\\,⟹\\,P=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡10x+10\\operatorname{sin}⁡10x.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265892 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bfe40da-51cf-5cfc-8bf3-d8d61eb492c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡12x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡12x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263115} {:answer/id #uuid "41137a18-3b7b-5a66-99b6-7227a71e6489" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡12x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263578} {:answer/id #uuid "45cd59f9-c985-59bb-b396-6d5cf9a8a8eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡12x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡12x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263613} {:answer/id #uuid "a7a7c280-30ea-5792-a4e6-5f3be8233ffd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡12x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡12x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264434} {:answer/id #uuid "e54d24eb-37ad-5a49-959c-d7dc616c5073" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡12x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264996}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0bfe40da-51cf-5cfc-8bf3-d8d61eb492c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡12x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡12x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263115} :answer-field/id #uuid "5179e9c4-31c5-5342-81c7-5cb9365f2374" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265392}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c1d3d599-7dfd-5eae-928a-1ef2cf2f900f" :question/math-academy-id "q-130356" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+144y=0,\\,y\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)=1,\\,{y}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)=24.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the roots of the characteristic polynomial:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+144 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-144 \\\\ \\lambda  & =\\pm 12\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =P\\operatorname{cos}⁡12x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡12x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe find the constants $P$ and $Q$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-Q=1\\,⟹\\,Q=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)=24,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-12P\\operatorname{sin}⁡12x+12Q\\operatorname{cos}⁡12x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)=24$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12P=24\\,⟹\\,P=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡12x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡12x.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357624 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30e2251b-7d16-5372-af31-a605bcd8d61d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355091} {:answer/id #uuid "35368f75-5659-5ae7-a5af-a8c1c96b7648" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355141} {:answer/id #uuid "5b39f1ae-f133-5b7b-a1db-74e10797637e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)-4\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355470} {:answer/id #uuid "8ec40822-5e09-542f-9d33-f9368a95d302" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)+4\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355923} {:answer/id #uuid "a525c814-3a04-5b28-90af-15cdaca6df19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356129}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a525c814-3a04-5b28-90af-15cdaca6df19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356129} :answer-field/id #uuid "c79cbe3f-3a7d-5248-b7e4-045c51d53800" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357277}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "169defb3-7918-5f63-aa50-008ef745a1e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-94020" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+2y=0,\\,y(0)=-4,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=4\\sqrt{2}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the roots of the characteristic polynomial:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+2 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-2 \\\\ \\lambda  & =\\pm \\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =P\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe find the constants $P$ and $Q$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=-4$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=4\\sqrt{2},$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-\\sqrt{2}P\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)+\\sqrt{2}Q\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=4\\sqrt{2}$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2}Q=4\\sqrt{2}\\,⟹\\,Q=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357625 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1454ed15-3ce0-5e04-ae1a-953b0729190a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡7x-7\\operatorname{sin}⁡7x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354842} {:answer/id #uuid "60170145-7906-582f-948b-4f0e5c7ba37d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡7x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡7x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355516} {:answer/id #uuid "95ce8d88-4046-546d-afb7-66bc070c0822" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡7x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡7x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355982} {:answer/id #uuid "b13a8fa9-9e11-5b64-aab8-06f2c5e18008" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡7x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡7x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356223} {:answer/id #uuid "c1d54fb8-e379-5bbf-9102-15ba7f5fdcfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡7x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡7x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356361}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95ce8d88-4046-546d-afb7-66bc070c0822" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡7x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡7x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355982} :answer-field/id #uuid "3379bea2-c2f3-5994-a403-3429a2cfa174" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357001}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "43040031-de84-5af2-ab15-84e08ad13676" :question/math-academy-id "q-94022" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+49y=0,\\,y(\\pi )=-2,\\,{y}^{′}(\\pi )=7.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the roots of the characteristic polynomial:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+49 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-49 \\\\ \\lambda  & =\\pm 7\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =P\\operatorname{cos}⁡7x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡7x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe find the constants $P$ and $Q$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(\\pi )=-2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-P=-2\\,⟹\\,P=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(\\pi )=7,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-7P\\operatorname{sin}⁡7x+7Q\\operatorname{cos}⁡7x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(\\pi )=7$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7Q=7\\,⟹\\,Q=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡7x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡7x.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357626 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4747d600-1d91-56c4-b391-7e39d8bd97a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡8x+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355296} {:answer/id #uuid "8d0219eb-bd91-5203-88e1-eadd21aaca30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡8x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355910} {:answer/id #uuid "9d5f477c-a221-585b-bb41-ef48d37a5087" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡8x-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356067} {:answer/id #uuid "ef182fc5-6118-53a3-929f-4809a418f978" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡8x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356748} {:answer/id #uuid "f1013af9-ccf4-5c49-bf03-e90fe4a1719c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡8x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356774}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4747d600-1d91-56c4-b391-7e39d8bd97a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡8x+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355296} :answer-field/id #uuid "988f17f9-6b54-55c6-a04d-62ad55586794" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357188}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b79961ad-edf6-5419-9f31-c0517e805a43" :question/math-academy-id "q-94023" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+64y=0,\\,y(\\pi )=1,\\,{y}^{′}(\\pi )=4.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the roots of the characteristic polynomial:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+64 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-64 \\\\ \\lambda  & =\\pm 8\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =P\\operatorname{cos}⁡8x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe find the constants $P$ and $Q$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(\\pi )=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(\\pi )=4,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-8P\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x+8Q\\operatorname{cos}⁡8x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(\\pi )=4$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8Q=4\\,⟹\\,Q=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{cos}⁡8x+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431531 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fc56a83-a0f5-5d43-aa8f-5d18e267ba12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{7}x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{7}x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431488} {:answer/id #uuid "924b9c7c-fba8-53a4-8c7d-12b59a208e50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{7}x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{7}x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431489} {:answer/id #uuid "ae7514f0-79da-5951-b071-38c575f33ed9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{7}x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{7}x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431497} {:answer/id #uuid "c65bb0d4-b401-58a8-9321-68e4246fafaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{7}x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{7}x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431505} {:answer/id #uuid "d575387f-ab5a-5abb-b0cd-aa50f48971a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{7}x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431510}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d575387f-ab5a-5abb-b0cd-aa50f48971a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{7}x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431510} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e73778b-1989-56f5-a344-4df7b08156a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431523}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "00d6379f-1cac-59b7-a19a-344de30af15c" :question/math-academy-id "q-130351" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+7y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{7}x)+B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{7}x),\n$$\n\nsolve the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+7y=0,\\,y(0)=-1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=-1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=0,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=A\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{7}x)-B\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{7}x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=0$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n0=A\\sqrt{7}\\,⟹\\,A=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{7}x).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431537 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b4c76a5-9a78-55cd-9899-c617f65dbb8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=11\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431463} {:answer/id #uuid "454410df-f8e1-54f6-9e27-a2798142e99e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡11x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431473} {:answer/id #uuid "4e27ee5a-1f56-520e-bd93-b277256b9d3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431476} {:answer/id #uuid "5b280312-42b5-5848-bb8a-62dfe17d7a2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431480} {:answer/id #uuid "c0ad627a-9899-5f34-94c4-32a5c8fa8625" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431504}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e27ee5a-1f56-520e-bd93-b277256b9d3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431476} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ac988a1-6644-54b0-ad8b-5e3dc0ec73cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431521}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b8669bf2-0ec8-592b-af07-c83c24aa14e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-130354" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+121y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11x)+B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11x),\n$$\n\nsolve the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+121y=0,\\,y(0)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=0,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=11A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11x)-11B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=0$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0=11A\\,⟹\\,A=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11x).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431540 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "067e7b03-611d-5b4d-b180-2ffdccf4d076" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431456} {:answer/id #uuid "59dfe9fd-988f-53c2-855f-b1614812537d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431479} {:answer/id #uuid "7428c405-4302-51f7-bc5d-fea12e12217f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431485} {:answer/id #uuid "aa31fab2-2bea-5ce6-a508-c29c038b4b72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431495} {:answer/id #uuid "f9d3393f-9411-5f1f-a0aa-92424adb8c2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431519}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7428c405-4302-51f7-bc5d-fea12e12217f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431485} :answer-field/id #uuid "408b0afd-e826-5064-a8e5-e44f09ba38cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431522}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e50b91c5-e53d-5ab3-9544-957263ee499e" :question/math-academy-id "q-81397" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+3y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}x)+B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{3}x),\n$$\n\nsolve the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+3y=0,\\,y(0)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=2\\sqrt{3}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=2\\sqrt{3},$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=A\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{3}x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=2\\sqrt{3}$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{3}=A\\sqrt{3}\\,⟹\\,A=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}x).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476932 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f302d50-9ca1-586e-b1f2-bb16774e9a32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476342} {:answer/id #uuid "7d1af17e-b2e8-5dca-b48a-32244e7c918d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476481} {:answer/id #uuid "9b5a0dcd-a0d2-5099-876c-b65c9f336a52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476540} {:answer/id #uuid "ca922ede-2598-5bbd-91ed-2c115cc7ea1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476658} {:answer/id #uuid "cfd949c2-5044-5076-a445-a9bbc18e3e7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476667}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f302d50-9ca1-586e-b1f2-bb16774e9a32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476342} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdeabe96-7dc2-5825-b44a-1ef489407f4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476869}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a134fdbb-21b9-55b4-a24e-2df884a5e2a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-81396" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+25y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=A\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x+B\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x,\n$$\n\nsolve the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+25y=0,\\,y(0)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=5.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=5,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=5A\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x-5B\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=5$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5=5A\\,⟹\\,A=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving Second-Order IVPs When the Characteristic Equation Has Imaginary Roots"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152287 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152008 :question/id #uuid "80968044-25e2-5906-929c-b944f84ca27d" :question/math-academy-id "e-7051" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\ny'' - 6y' + 25y=0, \\quad y(0)= 2,  \\quad y'(0) = 5.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the roots of the characteristic polynomial by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +25 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +9)-9+25 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)^{2}+16 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)^{2} & =-16 \\\\ \\lambda -3 & =\\pm 4\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =3\\pm 4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following general solution:\n\n$$\ny = e^{3x} \\left( P \\cos 4x + Q \\sin 4x \\right)\n$$\n\nWe find the constants $P$ and $Q$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0) = 2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n2 = P.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition $y'(0) = 5,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =3{e}^{3x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)+{e}^{3x}(-4P\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+4Q\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $y'(0) = 5$ and $P=2$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =3{e}^{0}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡0+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡0)+{e}^{0}(-4(2)\\operatorname{sin}⁡0+4Q\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\ 5 & =6+4Q \\\\ -1 & =4Q \\\\ Q & =-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny = e^{3x} \\left( 2 \\cos 4x - \\dfrac{1}{4} \\sin 4x \\right).\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "20e5f532-d99f-5406-b006-f34aa9074819" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152404 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d81758a1-467b-530b-82ed-1a512ef72718" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = e^{-x}(3\\cos 2x - \\sin 2x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148956} {:answer/id #uuid "d99d5a15-a222-54c7-bf19-f74127e55acf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = e^{-x}(3\\cos 2x + \\sin 2x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148957} {:answer/id #uuid "0a66397c-0490-5072-82c9-2d2240deff6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 3e^{-x}\\cos 2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148958} {:answer/id #uuid "0be5b4db-ddce-59e9-827e-5021dec2fd58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = e^{-2x}(3\\cos x - 5\\sin x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148959} {:answer/id #uuid "791b2684-a257-53cb-84b7-354943b2e2aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 5e^{-2x}\\sin x + 3\\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148960}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d81758a1-467b-530b-82ed-1a512ef72718" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = e^{-x}(3\\cos 2x - \\sin 2x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148956} :answer-field/id #uuid "90656c46-dd4f-5081-ac12-2c172a198ac4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148955}] :question/id #uuid "10337575-a96a-50d3-819b-452bcfd42d72" :question/math-academy-id "q-130534" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n$$\n\\displaystyle y^{″} + 2y^{′} + 5y = 0, y(0) = 3, y^{′}(0) =-5.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The characteristic equation is\n$$\n\\lambda^2+2\\lambda+5=(\\lambda+1)^2+4=0,\n$$\nwith roots $-1\\pm2\\mathrm{i}.$ Therefore,\n$$\ny=e^{-x}(P\\cos2x+Q\\sin2x).\n$$\nThe condition $y(0)=3$ gives $P=3.$ Differentiating gives\n$$\ny'=-e^{-x}(P\\cos2x+Q\\sin2x)+e^{-x}(-2P\\sin2x+2Q\\cos2x).\n$$\nUsing $y'(0)=-5$ gives $-P+2Q=-5,$ hence $Q=-1.$ Therefore,\n$$\ny=e^{-x}(3\\cos2x-\\sin2x).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152799 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a308af3-6719-5826-a24a-2f8b7b066053" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = e^{3x}(5\\cos 5x - \\sin 5x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151302} {:answer/id #uuid "b32ff3e1-6155-5fbd-942d-efef7165e8b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = e^{3x}(5\\cos 5x + \\sin 5x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151303} {:answer/id #uuid "d969a27a-0ed7-5196-a356-1aa74c7793e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = e^{3x}(5\\cos 5x - 2\\sin 5x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151304} {:answer/id #uuid "4af2db9f-dff0-536a-80a4-1b8399883298" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = e^{3x}(5\\cos 5x + 2\\sin 5x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151305} {:answer/id #uuid "5d4f9e59-0cd6-5a6a-961b-b231308bc97f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = e^{3x}(5\\cos 5x + 3\\sin 5x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151306}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a308af3-6719-5826-a24a-2f8b7b066053" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = e^{3x}(5\\cos 5x - \\sin 5x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151302} :answer-field/id #uuid "95e0e6f4-3bc8-5f22-a3b9-9a1139d085ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151301}] :question/id #uuid "2270856f-5217-52df-b9ab-69516b7671a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-7895" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n$y^{″} - 6y^{′} + 34y = 0$\n\nhas the general solution\n$y = e^{3x}(P\\cos 5x + Q\\sin 5x)$,\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n$$\n\\displaystyle y^{″} - 6y^{′} + 34y = 0, y(0) = 5, y^{′}(0) = 10.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The characteristic roots are $3\\pm5\\mathrm{i},$ so\n$$\ny=e^{3x}(P\\cos5x+Q\\sin5x).\n$$\nThe first condition gives $P=5.$ Differentiating,\n$$\ny'=3e^{3x}(P\\cos5x+Q\\sin5x)+e^{3x}(-5P\\sin5x+5Q\\cos5x).\n$$\nUsing $y'(0)=10$ gives $3P+5Q=10,$ hence $Q=-1.$ Therefore,\n$$\ny=e^{3x}(5\\cos5x-\\sin5x).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265896 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34d0b3d7-1d8f-587d-9211-8b2a3b1a51f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{4x}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡7x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡7x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263463} {:answer/id #uuid "49075e31-b783-554a-979a-16656dea3f98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{x}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡7x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡7x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263628} {:answer/id #uuid "b561879e-10c3-5ca4-8a8c-ece03fcdc678" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{4x}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡7x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡7x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264568} {:answer/id #uuid "f6632193-b888-59e0-9eb2-c53790a58ef0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{4x}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡7x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡7x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265156} {:answer/id #uuid "f82c0f99-b3cb-5191-b91e-666049ea9a2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{x}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡7x+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡7x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265171}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6632193-b888-59e0-9eb2-c53790a58ef0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{4x}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡7x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡7x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265156} :answer-field/id #uuid "90953058-5f2e-5e72-b3f9-b2688ceac8c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265504}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ca63aa49-385b-56ea-a947-ce7f0c3b0f73" :question/math-academy-id "q-130370" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-8{y}^{′}+65y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny={e}^{4x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡7x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡7x),\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-8{y}^{′}+65y=0,\\,y(0)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=1.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $P$ and $Q$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nP=2.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=1,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=4{e}^{4x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡7x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡7x)+{e}^{4x}(-7P\\operatorname{sin}⁡7x+7Q\\operatorname{cos}⁡7x).\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(0)=1$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n4P+7Q=1.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $P=2$ gives $Q=-1.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{4x}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡7x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡7x).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265897 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "225436c7-1040-53f2-b7c2-c93ed7f33de9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{x}(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263304} {:answer/id #uuid "6ec051e8-b7be-5edf-8bfd-854403ed4baa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{x}(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263961} {:answer/id #uuid "8c434f07-e607-5e49-be62-cec9d249a1b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{x}(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264200} {:answer/id #uuid "9f3d1530-1739-524a-be3b-17c859aca61e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{x}(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264357} {:answer/id #uuid "df1cdc63-fd87-52f5-82da-a33850cc513b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{x}(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264934}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c434f07-e607-5e49-be62-cec9d249a1b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{x}(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264200} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ebab9cc-10af-510a-bba4-26150c8fb35d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265466}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "daaabba6-e7df-5eda-aff7-b489684ff603" :question/math-academy-id "q-130371" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}+26y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny={e}^{x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x),\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}+26y=0,\\,y(0)=-4,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=1.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $P$ and $Q$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=-4$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nP=-4.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=1,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={e}^{x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x)+{e}^{x}(-5P\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x+5Q\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x).\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(0)=1$ into the above to get\n\n$$\nP+5Q=1.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $P=-4$ gives $Q=1.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{x}(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265898 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "505e2df8-db79-59e7-a583-99babc506741" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-x}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263697} {:answer/id #uuid "5654280f-88bb-59f1-b9d2-19091ada66cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263743} {:answer/id #uuid "79b176c8-c019-5f2d-89b9-2523faf24214" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-x}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264055} {:answer/id #uuid "d4e423e9-b332-5cd9-a6ed-b6e6e50a5c8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-x}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264852} {:answer/id #uuid "e7b0ac67-5324-577a-afe9-536d41e51116" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-x}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265018}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5654280f-88bb-59f1-b9d2-19091ada66cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263743} :answer-field/id #uuid "9cf4956a-8f92-55a5-93db-74651c950270" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265525}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c95764b1-5855-5fb2-b3ad-f0b7d5850b93" :question/math-academy-id "q-130374" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+2y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x),\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+2y=0,\\,y(0)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-2.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $P$ and $Q$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nP=2.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=-2,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-{e}^{-x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+{e}^{-x}(-P\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{cos}⁡x).\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(0)=-2$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n-P+Q=-2.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $P=2$ gives $Q=0.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348131 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f9690a7-a7e2-5397-9fab-5932d5f57697" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{2x}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345480} {:answer/id #uuid "259386fa-930c-5ed2-8146-0410d65c7c78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{e}^{2x}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345690} {:answer/id #uuid "3e1db9ec-13d0-523f-beab-84f5738731bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{e}^{2x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345876} {:answer/id #uuid "d42af497-46f2-5618-b60b-d642f0f7e4c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{2x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347206} {:answer/id #uuid "d6d750ad-e2fd-5a5b-a423-66b337485f92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{e}^{2x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347247}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6d750ad-e2fd-5a5b-a423-66b337485f92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{e}^{2x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347247} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6288fe0-74a5-5333-b0d5-8d242026b44c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347925}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9131a7ff-7e61-5a90-96bc-6b1cab75b7bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-7892" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-4{y}^{′}+8y=0,\\,y\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)={e}^{\\pi },\\text{ }\\text{ }{y}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)=4{e}^{\\pi }.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the roots of the characteristic polynomial by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +8 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +4)-4+8 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -2)^{2}+4 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -2)^{2} & =-4 \\\\ \\lambda -2 & =\\pm 2\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =2\\pm 2\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={e}^{2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe find the constants $P$ and $Q$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)={e}^{\\pi }$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-P{e}^{\\pi } & ={e}^{\\pi } \\\\ P & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)=4{e}^{\\pi },$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2{e}^{2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+{e}^{2x}(-2P\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+2Q\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)=4{e}^{\\pi }$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2P{e}^{\\pi }-2Q{e}^{\\pi } & =4{e}^{\\pi } \\\\ -2P-2Q & =4 \\\\ 2-2Q & =4 \\\\ Q & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $P=-1$ and $Q=-1.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={e}^{2x}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x) \\\\  & =-{e}^{2x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357627 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0038ad00-cbef-555c-b4ef-4c68141d3844" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-2x}(-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354658} {:answer/id #uuid "09bfb13a-5032-50df-8a5f-8f4a6c0a4bd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-2x}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354755} {:answer/id #uuid "2f5dcb2c-cea8-56b7-9456-0766f72b8509" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-2x}(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355075} {:answer/id #uuid "49966142-bc9a-56bd-a8a1-fa56c7efffc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-2x}(8\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355318} {:answer/id #uuid "c19a7e5b-8d42-5925-8bf0-cfa378fb7bd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2{e}^{-2x}(6\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356358}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0038ad00-cbef-555c-b4ef-4c68141d3844" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-2x}(-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354658} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc7a07ed-713b-5880-92ea-6cbd8e8d8cac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357287}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c3243450-c950-543f-968a-f0bf49df75ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-94025" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}+5y=0,\\,y\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)={e}^{-\\pi },\\,{y}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)=6{e}^{-\\pi }.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the roots of the characteristic polynomial by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +5 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +4)-4+5 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +2)^{2}+1 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +2)^{2} & =-1 \\\\ \\lambda +2 & =\\pm \\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =-2\\pm \\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={e}^{-2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe find the constants $P$ and $Q$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)={e}^{-\\pi }$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q{e}^{-\\pi } & ={e}^{-\\pi } \\\\ Q & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)=6{e}^{-\\pi },$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-2{e}^{-2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+{e}^{-2x}(-P\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{cos}⁡x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)=6{e}^{-\\pi }$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2Q{e}^{-\\pi }-P{e}^{-\\pi } & =6{e}^{-\\pi } \\\\ -2Q-P & =6 \\\\ -2-P & =6 \\\\ P & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $P=-8$ and $Q=1.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={e}^{-2x}(-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357628 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4de3cea3-9ce1-5117-8440-1c848ea22d4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-3x}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355356} {:answer/id #uuid "82b9aacb-816c-533f-8f18-7bad4adc1c9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-3x}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355814} {:answer/id #uuid "90f20f88-ad66-5e68-9ff3-f7c959e067cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-3x}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355943} {:answer/id #uuid "a0a0b4b1-1e9c-550c-b5cf-d7579feaa3f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-3x}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356089} {:answer/id #uuid "f366d31e-4d24-5d08-beff-fd3ad156a6d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-3x}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356793}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f366d31e-4d24-5d08-beff-fd3ad156a6d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-3x}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356793} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdfe16cc-d998-5278-adcf-1b050e572699" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357355}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ecd297d2-0d03-5232-81da-fdcaeb168238" :question/math-academy-id "q-94030" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+6{y}^{′}+13y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-3x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x),\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+6{y}^{′}+13y=0,\\,y(0)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-4.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $P$ and $Q$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nP=2.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=-4,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-3{e}^{-3x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+{e}^{-3x}(-2P\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+2Q\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x).\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(0)=-4$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n-3P+2Q=-4.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $P=2$ gives $Q=1.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-3x}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357629 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bbe7ab6-82e9-50b7-b0f3-51ff9e66eb25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-x}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355200} {:answer/id #uuid "79213f2d-f97b-5d4a-b314-892d34e6f483" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-x}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355723} {:answer/id #uuid "9b62b261-9912-5653-a744-887a7e9fd962" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-x}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356043} {:answer/id #uuid "c547990f-5ff0-5075-9227-f62d5e9174f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-x}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356390} {:answer/id #uuid "e8f69cf6-6441-5127-af8c-563c01d7f917" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-x}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356701}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79213f2d-f97b-5d4a-b314-892d34e6f483" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-x}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355723} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb04a8dc-50e7-5576-91a7-db21087a1bda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357255}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d3ff3059-40bc-5806-aa50-610fed058a26" :question/math-academy-id "q-94031" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+17y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x),\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+17y=0,\\,y(0)=-1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-11.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $P$ and $Q$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=-1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nP=-1.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=-11,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-{e}^{-x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)+{e}^{-x}(-4P\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+4Q\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x).\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(0)=-11$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n-P+4Q=-11.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $P=-1$ gives $Q=-3.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={e}^{-x}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431532 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b282211-1d23-5349-b3f7-ddda48199c41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{x-\\pi /6}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431468} {:answer/id #uuid "50868c33-8407-589c-bfad-291f32fb6f3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-x+\\pi /6}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431477} {:answer/id #uuid "9fa32848-af4f-5ffd-ad94-45426b415ba6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{x-\\pi /6}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431492} {:answer/id #uuid "bf0206d8-67a6-5880-99ad-0ae8bdd971eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-x+\\pi /6}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431502} {:answer/id #uuid "bfb9cf92-1a16-58f2-9b54-96a4a29652b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-x+\\pi /6}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431503}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50868c33-8407-589c-bfad-291f32fb6f3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-x+\\pi /6}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431477} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4eeea1c-8cea-5fa0-af41-255c4c40e45b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431529}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1a78761c-d0ad-5651-b02a-e973e2385ada" :question/math-academy-id "q-7893" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+10y=0,\\,y\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)=1,\\text{ }\\text{ }{y}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)=2.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+2\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+10{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +10) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +10=0.\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation can be solved by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +10 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +1)-1+10 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)^{2}+9 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)^{2} & =-9 \\\\ \\lambda +1 & =\\pm 3\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =-1\\pm 3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={e}^{-x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow let's find the constants $P$ and $Q.$ \n\nSubstituting $y\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q{e}^{-\\pi /6} & =1 \\\\ Q & ={e}^{\\pi /6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)=2.$ First, we differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}$:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-{e}^{-x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)+{e}^{-x}(-3P\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+3Q\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x)\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)=2$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-Q{e}^{-\\pi /6}-3P{e}^{-\\pi /6} & =2 \\\\ -Q-3P & =2{e}^{\\pi /6} \\\\ -{e}^{\\pi /6}-3P & =2{e}^{\\pi /6} \\\\ P & =-{e}^{\\pi /6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $Q={e}^{\\pi /6}$ and $P=-{e}^{\\pi /6}.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={e}^{-x}(-{e}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+{e}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x) \\\\  & ={e}^{-x+\\pi /6}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431535 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0db04b57-7e0b-51b5-9068-627b530d93d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2{e}^{x}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431461} {:answer/id #uuid "697fcea0-b422-5fd9-8a3c-b4de3653327a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2{e}^{x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431482} {:answer/id #uuid "a8ec0f9e-bd19-5a45-8045-94296328023e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431494} {:answer/id #uuid "c75b25a4-08bf-5b34-b13b-1d43f8125742" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-4{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431506} {:answer/id #uuid "c906702c-bb29-5e13-834a-3f940496c811" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2{e}^{-x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431507}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "697fcea0-b422-5fd9-8a3c-b4de3653327a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2{e}^{x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431482} :answer-field/id #uuid "aab4196f-6b76-5bce-9655-3bb0e187a2a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431527}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4d183a38-3bd7-5a3d-b0c0-6bbf656b9b64" :question/math-academy-id "q-130533" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}+2y=0,\\,y(0)=-2,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-4.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-2\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+2{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +2=0.\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation can be solved by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +2 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +1)-1+2 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -1)^{2}+1 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -1)^{2} & =-1 \\\\ \\lambda -1 & =\\pm \\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =1\\pm \\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x).\n$$\n\nNow let's find the constants $P$ and $Q.$ \n\nSubstituting $y(0)=-2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nP=-2.\n$$\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\ny={e}^{x}(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x).\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=-4.$ We differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}$:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={e}^{x}(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+{e}^{x}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=-4$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n-2+Q=-4\\,⟹\\,Q=-2.\n$$\n\nSo we have $P=-2$ and $Q=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-2{e}^{x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431536 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "676537c8-4285-5aad-a757-a9d82bb77416" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-2x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431481} {:answer/id #uuid "93f7ea21-c612-5811-b154-48179ccad499" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-2x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431490} {:answer/id #uuid "aa4bbbd3-9f33-5dfb-b89b-72bf0b2ad247" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-2x}\\left(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431496} {:answer/id #uuid "bc331650-5409-5760-9fea-61f15da13246" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-2x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431500} {:answer/id #uuid "d49931e9-d307-5540-8815-ad67d0cb20b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-2x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa4bbbd3-9f33-5dfb-b89b-72bf0b2ad247" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-2x}\\left(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431496} :answer-field/id #uuid "92b560c3-a3e3-5fae-81d1-ba12be4a1dcc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431526}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ad9f0a12-4237-5c82-9aa7-6fbbeb604773" :question/math-academy-id "q-94027" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}+13y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x),\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}+13y=0,\\,y(0)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-1.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $P$ and $Q$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nP=1.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=-1,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-2{e}^{-2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)+{e}^{-2x}(-3P\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+3Q\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x).\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(0)=-1$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n-2P+3Q=-1.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $P=1$ gives $Q=\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={e}^{-2x}\\left(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving Second-Order IVPs When the Characteristic Equation Has Complex Roots"}] :topic/math-academy-id 2741 :topic/title "Second-Order Homogeneous Initial Value Problems"}]}
